# Copy to `.env`. Vite only exposes variables prefixed `VITE_`, and only inlines
# them at build time — `pnpm run build` bakes these into the bundle, so changing
# one means rebuilding, not restarting. Nothing here is a secret: it all ships to
# the browser in plain text.

# Where the SPA sends every API call. Validated by @masdan/env/web at import, so a
# typo fails the build rather than surfacing as a runtime fetch error.
#
# "/" means same-origin: the API is reached on whatever origin served the page,
# via the /api/auth and /rpc proxy in apps/web/nginx.conf.template (and
# vite.config.ts's dev proxy locally). Keeping it relative is what lets one built
# image run in every environment. An absolute URL still works for a deployment
# that genuinely puts the API on another host. Not "" — an empty value reads as
# unset and fails validation.
VITE_SERVER_URL=/

# Dev server port. Read by apps/web/vite.config.ts, which also honours PORT.
# WEB_PORT=2600
